# Astra Deck release signing keys, in OpenSSH allowed_signers format.
#
# Every published release carries build/SHA256SUMS plus a detached
# build/SHA256SUMS.sig made with one of the keys below. Verifying that
# signature is what makes the checksum file a provenance claim rather than a
# corruption check: releases are built locally, so without it the artifacts and
# their hashes share one origin and forging both is one step.
#
# To verify a download, from the directory holding SHA256SUMS, SHA256SUMS.sig,
# and this file:
#
#   ssh-keygen -Y verify -f allowed-signers -I releases@astra-deck \
#     -n astra-deck-release -s SHA256SUMS.sig < SHA256SUMS
#   sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
#
# The first command proves who produced the list. The second proves your files
# match it. Both must pass.
#
# Format: <principal> <key-type> <key-body>
# The private half never enters this repository. See docs/signing-keys.md §9.
#
# No release signing key is published yet. Until a key line appears below,
# releases carry an unsigned checksum file and `npm run release:readiness`
# reports the gap as a warning rather than a failure. See Roadmap_Blocked.md.
